<title>USA: Equity Inns says buys 2 hotels for $14.5 mln.</title>
<headline>Equity Inns says buys 2 hotels for $14.5 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MEMPHIS, Tenn. 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Equity Inns Inc said Thursday it acquired a Homewood Suites in suburban Memphis and a Hampton Inn in Destin, Fla. for $14.5 million with a combination of cash and partnership units.</p>
<p>The Homewood Suites has 92 suites and the Hampton Inn has 90 rooms and 14 suites.</p>
<p>The company said it has bought 37 properties since January, and it remains &quot;well ahead&quot; of analysts' projections in this area.</p>
<p>Memphis-based Equity Inns is a real estate investment trust.</p>
</text>
